  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Atlas Air has $565M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Atlas Air won 339 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $1.7M and obligations down 25.6% year over year. Atlas Air obligations peaked in FY25 at $759M and remain material this year, with FY26 obligations totaling $565M. Atlas Air also recorded smaller obligations in earlier years: FY21 $13.5M, FY22 $1.7M, FY23 $6M, and FY24 $3.7M. Atlas Air derives most FY2026 to date revenue from Nonscheduled Chartered Passenger Air Transportation at $563M. Atlas Air recorded other FY2026 to date market obligations including Scheduled Freight Air Transportation $1.1M, Other Technical and Trade Schools $333K, and Flight Training $332K. The current-year totals are fiscal year to date and represent contract obligations, while the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables use total contract values rather than obligated amounts.",
